[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441941683","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4262#issuecomment-441941683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4262","id":441941683,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTk0MTY4Mw==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-05-21T13:28:16Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:21:17Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nhi there -\n\nthis bug report is lacking detail, namely a test case or any description what it is you're trying to do, so I grepped a bit to try to understand what you might be doing.\n\n \"_default_dialect\" is a method that is called upon only when type.compile() is called or you call str(type) on the object.   Since this is a third party type, it should be expected that it would not have a stringify without an explicit dialect being passed, as detailed at http://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/faq/sqlexpressions.html#how-do-i-render-sql-expressions-as-strings-possibly-with-bound-parameters-inlined.\n\nthat said, the case of datatypes has historically been a bit special, as there may have been some poorly defined cases within the library where str() was being called on type objects internally.   But, I'd hope those are all gone by now (but, I could be wrong).\n\nTBH, what I see _default_dialect() doing right now I'm not completely comfortable with and this looks like it was a hack added in 0.6 to provide backwards compatibility with 0.5.    Adding a whole new third-party dialect lookup system here that makes assumptions about how those dialects work and gives no indication that it might not be using the correct type compiler will lead to silent bugs.  \n\nAnyway, I need to know why you need to stringify type objects without a dialect being given to better understand what should be done here.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441941683/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https: